<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Currency Converter website</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="tic.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>Currency Converter by viratkoshta</h1>
    <p>Convert money using a exchange rate API</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="converter-box">
      <h2>Convert your money</h2>
      <p>Enter an amount, choose two currencies, and press convert.</p>

      <label for="amount">Amount</label>
      <input id="amount" type="number" value="1" min="0" step="any">

      <div class="currency-row">
        <div>
          <label for="from-currency">From</label>
          <select id="from-currency"></select>
        </div>

        <button class="swap-button" id="swap" type="button" aria-label="Swap currencies">⇄</button>

        <div>
          <label for="to-currency">To</label>
          <select id="to-currency"></select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <button class="convert-button" id="convert" type="button">Convert</button>

      <div class="result" aria-live="polite">
        <p>Your converted amount</p>
        <div id="result">Loading...</div>
        <p id="rate-info">Getting the latest exchange rate.</p>
      </div>

      <p id="message" role="status"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-box">
      <h2>How this website works</h2>
      <p>This project uses an API to get the latest exchange rate instead of using fixed values.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>JavaScript sends a request using <code>fetch()</code>.</li>
        <li>The API sends back the exchange rate as JSON data.</li>
        <li>The website multiplies your amount by that rate.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>Made as a simple currency converter project &middot; Rates from Frankfurter API</footer>

  <script src="tic.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
